# KCALL_RESIZE (roadmap os-server.md P15): a segment made longer in place
# over memory a revoke left written, its copy with it, its bytes kept and
# the new ones zeroed in pieces; every refusal; shorter, its end retyped
# next; a read past a shorter end through ES, loaded before the call, is
# the program's fault. tests/programs/additions.asm, TEST_ADD_RESIZE.
program: additions
define: TEST_CAPS
define: TEST_ADD_RESIZE
match: contains
timeout: 60
---
additions: make it 8,000 bytes (0): 0
additions: its copy's limit (7999): 7999
additions: its base kept (1): 1
additions: the word at its old end, through the copy (4660): 4660
additions: its new bytes, ORed (0): 0
additions: resize the copy (6): 6
additions: past its untyped (3): 3
additions: to 0 bytes (2): 2
additions: its own data, of the root's untyped (6): 6
additions: an untyped (1): 1
additions: sealed code (2): 2
additions: make it 100 bytes (0): 0
additions: its copy's limit (99): 99
additions: the next retype's base, from its (112: its end given back): 112
additions: longer, with that carved after it (6): 6
additions: a read past a shorter end, through ES loaded before
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0007:{resize_part.read_f}
additions: done
